<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Mesh on SWITNEX</title><link>https://www.switnex.com/tags/mesh/</link><description>Recent content in Mesh on SWITNEX</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 10 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.switnex.com/tags/mesh/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Weak gateway signal — quick checks</title><link>https://www.switnex.com/troubleshooting/2026/05/10/gateway-signal/</link><pubDate>Sun, 10 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.switnex.com/troubleshooting/2026/05/10/gateway-signal/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Goes with the &lt;strong&gt;Troubleshooting&lt;/strong&gt; hub item about devices dropping offline. Do the hub steps first, then skim the FAQ below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage"&gt;
&lt;div class="accordion-item switnex-ts-faq-item border-0 shadow-sm mb-2 rounded overflow-hidden" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"&gt;
 &lt;h2 class="accordion-header h5 mb-0"&gt;
 &lt;button class="accordion-button collapsed py-3" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq-0-108facb05c4d570159fa1c55d42bd084" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-0-108facb05c4d570159fa1c55d42bd084"&gt;
 &lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Move the hub first or add a repeater?&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;div id="faq-0-108facb05c4d570159fa1c55d42bd084" class="accordion-collapse collapse" role="region"&gt;
 &lt;div class="accordion-body border-top" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"&gt;
 &lt;div itemprop="text"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change one thing at a time.&lt;/strong&gt; Move the hub or a plug-in repeater closer to the weak spot with fewer walls in between. Rule out metal cabinets and microwaves before buying more gear.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="accordion-item switnex-ts-faq-item border-0 shadow-sm mb-2 rounded overflow-hidden" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"&gt;
 &lt;h2 class="accordion-header h5 mb-0"&gt;
 &lt;button class="accordion-button collapsed py-3" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq-1-108facb05c4d570159fa1c55d42bd084" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-1-108facb05c4d570159fa1c55d42bd084"&gt;
 &lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Can Wi-Fi channel changes hurt Zigbee?&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;div id="faq-1-108facb05c4d570159fa1c55d42bd084" class="accordion-collapse collapse" role="region"&gt;
 &lt;div class="accordion-body border-top" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"&gt;
 &lt;div itemprop="text"&gt;Yes — both often use 2.4 GHz. Try a fixed Wi-Fi channel, or put the USB stick on an extension cable away from the router.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="switnex-upgrade-banner card border-0 shadow-sm my-4" role="complementary"&gt;
 &lt;div class="card-body d-flex flex-column flex-md-row gap-3 align-items-md-center"&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex-grow-1"&gt;
 &lt;h3 class="h6 fw-bold mb-2"&gt;&lt;i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-trend-up me-2 text-warning" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Hardware a few years old?&lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;div class="small text-body-secondary mb-0"&gt;Sometimes it’s cheaper to upgrade than to fight an old coordinator. Email your model and where you bought it.&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="flex-shrink-0"&gt;
